 for a  year and a couple months it's been very  effective and now we need to make sure  that we continue to do that so that we  ultimately get the opportunity to  convince Iran  it's not in their best interest to  behave in this way we all have to  remember this isn't just two and a half  years or five years this is 40 years of  Iranian activity that has led us to this  point and to reestablish deterrence is a  challenge but one that I know the Trump  administration is up to and we're  working hard each and every day both in  the State Department and the Department  of Defense and all the elements the  United States government to achieve that  and with that I'm happy to take a couple  questions yes ma'am  the situation almost certainly President  Trump had sent president Ave to take a  message of his to the leadership in Iran  you have to remember these are messages  for the leadership I think the Iranian  people are being woefully Mis served by  that leadership but yes we're engaged in  we have been engaged in many messages  even this this moment right here  communicating to Iran that we are there  to deter aggression President Trump does  not want war and we will continue to  communicate that message while doing the  things that are necessary to protect  American interests in the region will  continue to provide additional  information about those attacks we  shouldn't focus on just those two  attacks there since the beginning of May  there are now over a half dozen  different instances of Iranian attacks  in the region some thwarted some not not  successfully thwarted next they had an  impact but I saw just as I walked in  here Chancellor Merkel say that she  thought there was strong evidence that  Iran had engaged in this activity will  continue to work with partners all  around the world it's worth reminding  everyone here you have China that  depends enormous ly on energy transiting  the Strait of Hormuz you have South  Korea Indonesia Japan all of whom have 